/F1 12 Tf
16 TL
1 0 0 1 72 667 Tm
(Owner: Tomas Bergqvist, Data Governance Lead) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
14.5 TL
1 0 0 1 72 644 Tm
(This standard states how long Northwind Cartography keeps each class of record, who is) Tj
T*
(accountable for the deletion of that class, and how the deletion is evidenced. It) Tj
T*
(applies to production systems, analytics warehouses, backups and third-party) Tj
T*
(processors. It replaces version 1.6 of 12 June 2023, which did not cover the analytics) Tj
T*
(warehouse.) Tj
/F1 12 Tf
16 TL
1 0 0 1 72 560.5 Tm
(Principles) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
14.5 TL
1 0 0 1 72 537.5 Tm
(- Collect the minimum. A field that is not collected does not have to be retained,) Tj
T*
(protected or deleted.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
14.5 TL
1 0 0 1 72 503.5 Tm
(- Retain for a stated purpose. Every retention period in this standard names the) Tj
T*
(purpose that justifies it.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
14.5 TL
1 0 0 1 72 469.5 Tm
(- Delete on a schedule, not on request. Deletion is automated so that it happens) Tj
T*
(whether or not anyone remembers.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
14.5 TL
1 0 0 1 72 435.5 Tm
(- Prove it. Each deletion run writes an evidence record that is itself retained for) Tj
T*
(three years.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
14.5 TL
1 0 0 1 72 401.5 Tm
(Retention periods in this standard are maximums. A team may hold a record for less) Tj
T*
(time than the maximum, and several do, but no team may hold a record for longer) Tj
T*
(without an approved legal hold.) Tj
/F1 12 Tf
16 TL
1 0 0 1 72 347 Tm
(Accountability) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
14.5 TL
1 0 0 1 72 324 Tm
(The Data Governance Lead owns this standard. Each retention class has a named) Tj
T*
(accountable team, listed in the schedule on page 2. The security team audits a sample) Tj
T*
(of deletions each quarter and reports the result to the risk committee, which meets on) Tj
T*
(the second Tuesday of February, May, August and November.) Tj
/F1 8 Tf
1 0 0 1 72 48 Tm
(Northwind Cartography - Data Retention Standard v2.0) Tj
