/F1 12 Tf
16 TL
1 0 0 1 72 690 Tm
(The monthly purge) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
14.5 TL
1 0 0 1 72 667 Tm
(The automated purge job runs on the fifth day of every month at 02:00 UTC. It walks) Tj
T*
(each retention class in the schedule, deletes the records that have passed their) Tj
T*
(maximum period, and writes a signed evidence record giving the class, the row count) Tj
T*
(and the job identifier. A purge that fails is retried once; a second failure pages the) Tj
T*
(Platform Engineering on-call rotation.) Tj
/F1 12 Tf
16 TL
1 0 0 1 72 583.5 Tm
(Legal holds) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
14.5 TL
1 0 0 1 72 560.5 Tm
(A legal hold suspends deletion for the records it names and overrides every period in) Tj
T*
(this standard. Only the General Counsel may place or release a hold, and every open) Tj
T*
(hold is reviewed at the quarterly risk committee meeting. Records under hold are) Tj
T*
(tagged in place rather than copied, so that a released hold returns the records to) Tj
T*
(their normal schedule automatically.) Tj
/F1 12 Tf
16 TL
1 0 0 1 72 477 Tm
(Customer deletion requests) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
14.5 TL
1 0 0 1 72 454 Tm
(A verified customer request to delete personal data is handled inside the window given) Tj
T*
(in the Information Security Policy and is fulfilled by the same purge machinery,) Tj
T*
(running out of cycle. The requester receives a written confirmation naming each) Tj
T*
(retention class that was cleared and each class that was retained under a legal or tax) Tj
T*
(obligation.) Tj
/F1 12 Tf
16 TL
1 0 0 1 72 370.5 Tm
